1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:11,634
Spirits of the Wild is a quick game for two players. Collect colorful stones, give them to five forest animals, and score the most points. Here's everything you need, in about four minutes.

2
00:00:12,299 --> 00:00:19,638
To set up, put all fifty six stones in the bag, and draw four into the bowl. If you draw a clear Spirit Stone, put it back.

3
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:30,646
Each player gets a board with five animals, and six action cards. Shuffle the Spirit cards into two piles, and the first player turns their Take Two Stones card face down.

4
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:36,697
On your turn, play one face-up action card, then turn it face down. Let's follow Ana.

5
00:00:37,366 --> 00:00:41,846
Take One Stone. She takes the red stone from the bowl, and gives it to her Rabbit.

6
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,681
Take Two Stones takes two at once. Two whites for her Turtle: three points.

7
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:52,325
Add Two Stones and Take One. First, two new stones go from the bag into the bowl.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,389
Then she takes one. Yellow, for the Rabbit.

9
00:00:56,066 --> 00:01:01,016
Add Three Stones and Move Coyote. Three stones go into the bowl, but she takes none.

10
00:01:01,666 --> 00:01:08,194
Instead, she sends the Coyote to one of Ben's animals. While it sits there, Ben can't add stones to his Turtle.

11
00:01:08,866 --> 00:01:15,138
Four of Ana's cards are now face down. Once at least three are, she may play her last card: Spirit Power.

12
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,256
She chooses one of the two Spirit cards on top. The Wolf.

13
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:22,066
The Wolf adds four stones to the bowl...

14
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:23,885
...and she takes one.

15
00:01:24,566 --> 00:01:33,206
Then the Spirit card goes under its pile, and all her action cards flip face up again. That's the rhythm of the game: spend your cards, then recover.

16
00:01:33,866 --> 00:01:37,578
Now, the five animals. Each one wants a different pattern of colors.

17
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:44,185
The Rabbit wants three different colors. A full set is worth six points. Anything less scores nothing.

18
00:01:44,866 --> 00:01:50,306
The Turtle wants one color only. More stones, more points: up to fourteen for five.

19
00:01:50,966 --> 00:01:56,129
The Salmon is the opposite: every stone a different color. All six colors earn thirteen.

20
00:01:56,799 --> 00:02:00,661
The Owl loves pairs. Each pair of the same color is worth four.

21
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:09,247
The Beaver wants three of a kind and a pair. Five, plus two, plus a seven point bonus for finishing both. Fourteen in total.

22
00:02:09,899 --> 00:02:15,830
A stone must fit the animal you give it to. If it fits nowhere on your board, it goes back to the bowl.

23
00:02:16,499 --> 00:02:21,193
The clear Spirit Stones are special. They only go on an animal's times-two space.

24
00:02:21,866 --> 00:02:29,226
They double that animal. This Turtle jumps from nine to eighteen points. But the animal is now closed: no more stones.

25
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:34,763
One more Coyote trick. Each Take One Stone card has half a Coyote on its back.

26
00:02:35,433 --> 00:02:38,739
When Ben turns both face down, the Coyote is complete...

27
00:02:39,399 --> 00:02:41,938
...and he may move it to any animal on Ana's board.

28
00:02:42,599 --> 00:02:53,799
There are six Spirit cards in all, each a different boost: more stones to choose from, stones straight from the bag, a swap, or even an extra turn. The reference video covers each one.

29
00:02:54,466 --> 00:03:01,741
The clear stones are also the clock. When five Spirit Stones are out of the bag at the end of a turn, the game ends right away.

30
00:03:02,399 --> 00:03:10,186
Add up your animals. The most points wins. And in a tie, whoever has the Coyote on their board wins. The trickster pays you back!

31
00:03:10,866 --> 00:03:18,951
That's it: play a card, feed your animals, recover with a Spirit power, and watch out for the Coyote. Now, let's watch a real game.
